## 3. The transaction

Prospective importation of Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257, produced as described in sections 4 and 5, exported from [FILL IN: country of exportation]. CBP has ruled on the current production setup: origin China (N328954). This request concerns a proposed change to that setup: make Motor-fan assembly and PCBA (SMT) in Thailand. [FILL IN: expected date of the first shipment].

## 4. The merchandise

- Name and model: Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257.
- Description: A 1500-watt heat gun with two fan speeds and a variable temperature control dial, used for heat shrinking, stripping paint and bending plastic.
- HTSUS subheading, for reference (classification is not requested): 8419.89.95.
- Proposed origin marking of the article and its container: [FILL IN: wording, method and location; attach illustrations].

## 5. Materials, countries and processing

Components and where each is made:

- main housing: Thailand (Rayong plant).
- electric motor: Thailand (Rayong plant).
- printed circuit board assembly (PCBA): Thailand (Rayong plant).
- power cord: China (China suppliers).
- switch: Malaysia (bought in).

Production steps and where each takes place:

- wind the motor stator and assemble the motor-fan unit: Rayong plant, Thailand.
- fasten the PCBA to the main housing and connect it to the motor: Rayong plant, Thailand.

Production as described:

The motor-fan assembly and PCBA are made in Thailand. Final assembly in Thailand.

[FILL IN: cost or share of value of each component, and the time and skill each step takes, if available].

## 6. Question presented

What is the country of origin of Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257, produced as described above, under substantial transformation (19 C.F.R. § 134.1(b)), for purposes of country of origin marking and Section 301 duties?

## 7. Requester's position and supporting authority

The requester submits that the merchandise is a product of Thailand, based on these key factors: motor-fan assembly made in Thailand and PCBA populated in Thailand. [FILL IN: the legal basis, with counsel].

Earlier CBP rulings relied on (19 C.F.R. § 177.2(b)(6)):

- N347421 — a comparable change where CBP found the origin moved ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N347421)).
- N345859 — a similar change that did not alter origin; distinguish it ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N345859)).
- N350001 ([rulings.cbp.gov](https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N350001)).

